        "code": "// You can open a \"Tailable Cursor\" on a capped collection.\n// It stays open and streams new data as it arrives, \n// similar to the 'tail -f' command in Linux.\nconst cursor = db.log.find().addOption(DBQuery.Option.tailable);",
        "tip": "Because they maintain strict insertion order natively, you rarely need an index on a capped collection to sort by time, making writes extremely fast.",
