        "title": "What is indexing?",
        "category": "Data Modeling, Relationships & Indexing",
        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "Indexing is the creation of a specialized data structure (a B-Tree) that stores a small portion of the collection's data set in an easy-to-traverse form. It allows the database engine to find specific documents quickly without having to scan every single document in the collection.",
        "example": "The Book Analogy.",
        "code": "// Without Index:\n// To find all users named 'Alice', MongoDB reads 1 million user docs. (COLLSCAN)\n\n// With Index on 'name':\n// MongoDB goes to the Index (like the index at the back of a book), \n// finds 'Alice', and goes directly to her exact disk location. (IXSCAN)",
