        "explanation": "Query optimization is the process of improving query performance. In MongoDB, this primarily involves:\n1. Creating effective compound indexes following the **ESR Rule** (Equality fields first, Sort fields second, Range fields last).\n2. Using Projection to return only necessary fields.\n3. Avoiding `$where` or regex queries not anchored to the front of a string.\n4. Denormalizing data to avoid `$lookup`.",
