        "title": "How do you avoid document growth issues?",
        "category": "Bonus: Top 75 Frequently Asked Senior-Level MongoDB Questions",
        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "Document growth occurs when arrays inside a document expand continuously (e.g., adding comments to a post). To avoid hitting the 16MB limit or causing excessive disk relocation:\n1. **Use the Outlier Pattern:** Embed the first 100 comments, push the rest to a separate `comments_overflow` collection.\n2. **Use Parent Referencing:** Stop embedding entirely and have comments reference the Post ID.\n3. **Use Bucketing:** Group data into chunks of 500 items per document.",
        "example": "The Outlier Pattern.",
