        "category": "Bonus: Top 75 Frequently Asked Senior-Level MongoDB Questions",
        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "When you run an aggregation, MongoDB parses the pipeline into an execution tree. The query optimizer attempts to reorganize the stages to improve performance. For example, if you place a `$sort` after a `$match`, the optimizer will ensure the `$match` uses indexes first. Data flows through the stages in memory, up to a 100MB limit per stage (unless `allowDiskUse` is true).",
