        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "MongoDB uses **B-Tree** (Balanced Tree) data structures for its indexes. A B-Tree stores the index keys in a sorted, hierarchical tree format. When a query is executed, the database traverses the tree from the root node down to the leaf nodes. Each leaf node contains the index key and a pointer (Record ID) to the actual physical document on the disk.",
