        "category": "Bonus: Top 75 Frequently Asked Senior-Level MongoDB Questions",
        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "A 'Covered Query' is a query that can be completely satisfied using ONLY the B-Tree index, without ever needing to fetch the actual document from the physical disk. This happens when the query criteria and the projection only include fields that are part of the index.",
